---

What this license covers: the knowledge graph — `data/*.yaml` (the source of
truth), the generated bundle, and the public exports (`static/dataset.json`,
`static/positions.csv`, `static/relationships.csv`, `static/sources.csv`, the
geographic layers and the changelog).

What it does not cover:

  - The code that builds and displays the graph — licensed under MIT, see
    `../LICENSE`.
  - The underlying cited sources (gazette entries, articles, archives), which
    remain under their own terms. This license covers DeepTunisia's selection,
    arrangement, translations and original prose — not the third-party
    material the citations point to.
  - Facts. Facts are not copyrightable; what is licensed here is the curated
    compilation and its analytical framing.

Attribution practice:

  DeepTunisia's own citation model is stronger than any license requires:
  every claim in the dataset names the sources it rests on, in `data/sources.yaml`
  and in the published exports. If you reuse the graph, attribute it to
  deeptunisia.org and link to the /data page — and when you redistribute,
  keep the per-claim citations attached so the record stays verifiable.
